PHASEX:  [P]hase [H]armonic [A]dvanced [S]ynthesis [EX]periment


MINIMUM REQUIREMENTS:
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Required:
	gcc-4.x (or clang)
	cmake-3.13
	gtk-2.4
	alsa-0.9.0
	jack-0.99.0
	libsamplerate-0.1.2

Optional:
	liblo (for NSM / New Session Manager support)

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------


OBTAINING PHASEX SOURCES:
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Currently, PHASEX dev sources are only available via git:

	git clone https://github.com/williamweston/phasex.git

RPM and .tar.gz packages will be made available with the
upcoming v0.15.0 stable release.


COMPILING AND INSTALLING PHASEX:
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Start in toplevel source directory:

	cd phasex

PHASEX uses CMake.  For a default configuration (which is probably
not what you want):

	cmake -S . -B build
	cmake --build build
	sudo cmake --install build

For a multitimbral build optimized for your CPU you might want to run:

	cmake -S . -B build -DPHASEX_NATIVE_ARCH=ON -DPHASEX_NUM_PARTS=2
	cmake --build build
	sudo cmake --install build

Useful CMake options (pass as -D<option>=<value>):

	CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE       Release (default), Debug, or RelWithDebInfo.
	CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX   Installation prefix (default /usr/local).
	PHASEX_NATIVE_ARCH     Build with -march=native -mtune=native (default OFF).
	PHASEX_CPU_POWER       CPU utilization: 1 (slow CPU), 2 (average CPU),
	                       3 (fast CPU and 32-bit sample_t), and 4 (fast
	                       CPU and 64-bit sample_t).  Default 2.
	PHASEX_NUM_PARTS       Number of active synth parts / threads (1-12).
	                       In general, enabling one part per CPU core will
	                       provide rock-solid xrun-free performance
	                       (recommended for live / on-stage use).  Modern
	                       multi-core systems may perform the same with as
	                       many as two synth threads per CPU core enabled
	                       (recommended for studio use).  As usual, YMMV.
	                       Default 1.
	PHASEX_WITH_LIBRT      Link against librt if needed for clock_gettime()
	                       and clock_nanosleep() (default ON).
	PHASEX_WITH_NSM        Build with New/Non Session Manager (NSM) support.
	                       Auto-disabled with a warning if liblo isn't found
	                       (default ON).

Examples:

	cmake -S . -B build \
	      -DPHASEX_CPU_POWER=1 \
	      -DPHASEX_NUM_PARTS=1

	cmake -S . -B build \
	      -DPHASEX_NATIVE_ARCH=ON \
	      -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug \
	      -DPHASEX_NUM_PARTS=4

For custom builds, additional settings may be configured in
src/phasex.h.  For most builds, modifiying phasex.h should not be
necessary.

